sections.content:
Stepanić je zatim pokazao pozadinske aplikacije na računalu u Lomnici. Neke se od njih pokreću više puta dnevno. Ključna je mali **WhatsApp bridge**, koji sam po sebi nije nikakav AI. To je mali backend koji se vrti u pozadini i autoriziran je njegovim brojem mobitela, isto kao službeni WhatsApp Desktop tvrtke Meta. Zajednica je reverse-engineeringom obradila WhatsAppov API i postoji open source rješenje za spajanje vlastite aplikacije. Na to je zajednica dodala i **MCP**.

MCP-ove ponovno opisuje kao male dodatke za Claude Code, ali i za **Antigravity** i **Codex**. Antigravity je, kaže, „Claude Code od Googlea”, a Codex „Claude Code od OpenAI-ja”. Među njegovim MCP-ovima su:
- **Jira**: za klijenta koji koristi Jiru za upravljanje projektima Claude sam piše poruke i na tikete upisuje što je napravljeno;
- dodaci za blockchain provjeru, dizajn i LinkedIn (za potonji priznaje da možda ne radi najbolje);
- **WhatsApp MCP**;
- **Gmail MCP**: nakon obavljenog posla dovoljno je reći „složi mi mail i pošalji ga odmah”;
- dodaci za Google kalendar, Google Drive, Magisterijum AI i Podscan FM.

Posebno je predstavio vlastiti **Domovina AI MCP**. Uz njega se svi podcasti na platformi mogu pametno pretraživati unutar Claude Codea ili Claude Desktopa. U pozadini je **semantička vektorska baza** sa stotinama tisuća poglavlja iz više od 3.000 podcasta. Može se tražiti, primjerice, gdje se u svim podcastima spominje Lenovo laptop, uz šalu da time „reklamira Lenovo”, ili rijeka Dunav.

Takva pretraga, ističe Stepanić, još nije dostupna ni u Geminiju. Gemini radi poput Google, odnosno YouTube pretrage: ne ulazi u sam sadržaj videa, nego gleda naslov i opis. Domovina AI može pronaći ne samo epizode u kojima je neka osoba bila gost ili voditelj, nego i one u kojima ju je netko od sugovornika **spomenuo**. Naglašava da ni vektorske baze nisu novost nastala s AI revolucijom. Instalirati se, zaključuje, može što god korisniku padne na pamet, od Figme nadalje.

sections.content_en:
Stepanić then showed the background applications on the computer in Lomnica. Some of them run multiple times a day. The key one is a small **WhatsApp bridge**, which in itself is not any AI. It is a small backend that runs in the background and is authorized with his mobile phone number, just like the official WhatsApp Desktop of the company Meta. The community reverse-engineered WhatsApp's API, and there is an open source solution for connecting one's own application. Onto that, the community also added an **MCP**.

He again describes MCPs as small add-ons for Claude Code, but also for **Antigravity** and **Codex**. Antigravity is, he says, „Claude Code from Google”, and Codex „Claude Code from OpenAI”. Among his MCPs are:
- **Jira**: for a client who uses Jira for project management, Claude itself writes messages and records on tickets what was done;
- add-ons for blockchain verification, design, and LinkedIn (for the latter, he admits that it might not work the best);
- **WhatsApp MCP**;
- **Gmail MCP**: after the work is done, it is enough to say „compose an email for me and send it right away”;
- add-ons for Google Calendar, Google Drive, Magisterijum AI, and Podscan FM.

He specifically presented his own **Domovina AI MCP**. With it, all podcasts on the platform can be smartly searched within Claude Code or Claude Desktop. In the background is a **semantic vector database** with hundreds of thousands of chapters from more than 3,000 podcasts. One can search, for example, where a Lenovo laptop is mentioned across all podcasts, along with a joke that by doing so he is „advertising Lenovo”, or the Danube River.

Such a search, Stepanić points out, is not yet available even in Gemini. Gemini works like Google, or rather YouTube search: it does not enter into the video content itself, but looks at the title and description. Domovina AI can find not only episodes in which a person was a guest or host, but also those in which one of the interlocutors **mentioned** them. He emphasizes that vector databases are not a novelty that arose with the AI revolution either. Whatever comes to the user's mind can be installed, he concludes, from Figma onwards.

sections.content:
Na kraju ovog dijela Stepanić je pokazao kako upravlja **duljinom konteksta**. Postavio je limit: kada kontekst prijeđe **180.000 tokena**, Claude mu predlaže da pozove **wrap-up skill**. Taj skill sažme sve što je trenutno u kontekstu modela, spremi to na disk i izradi **handoff prompt** za nastavak rada u sljedećoj sesiji.

Skill je napravio uz pomoć Claudea i dostupan je na **stepanic.domovina.ai** te na njegovu **GitHubu**. Riječ je o većoj količini teksta s uputama. Sve što se odvija u chatu nije trajno spremljeno na disk, a Claude tijekom rada nauči mnogo detalja: koje su zamke, što je još otvoreno i slično. Naredba `/wrap-up` prođe kroz cijeli razgovor, zabilježi te stvari i u kućnom direktoriju, u mapi za handoffove, stvori datoteku s točnim uputama kako nastaviti.

Zašto je to korisno? Stepanić tvrdi da je **Claude najbolji kada sam sebi piše promptove**. Takav je prompt optimalno složen: troši minimalno tokena, a daje najbolji rezultat u sljedećoj sesiji. To je posebno važno pri radu s više paralelnih Claude Code sesija.

Podijelio je i vlastita zapažanja o kontekstu:
- u trenutku demonstracije sesija je trošila **101.000 tokena** od raspoloživih milijun;
- prva poruka odmah zauzme oko **60.000 tokena**, jer se u kontekst učita mnoštvo skillova i drugih podataka;
- prvih 100.000 tokena popunjava se puno brže, a kasnije svaka poruka dodaje tek malo;
- ako se ubaci velika količina vlastitog znanja, kontekst može narasti i na 600.000 tokena;
- alat je, prema njegovu iskustvu, najučinkovitiji oko **220.000 do 250.000 tokena**, a sljedeći limit na koji pazi jest 300.000.

Rad tako dijeli u cjeline. Kada je jedna gotova i vidi da sve radi, pokrene wrap-up, zatim očisti sesiju naredbom `clear`. U novoj sesiji ne mora predavati nikakvu datoteku: dovoljno je reći „nastavi sa zadnjim handoffom”, jer je i za to napravio poseban skill.

sections.content_en:
At the end of this part, Stepanić showed how he manages **context length**. He set a limit: when the context exceeds **180,000 tokens**, Claude suggests to him that he call the **wrap-up skill**. That skill summarizes everything that is currently in the model's context, saves it to disk, and creates a **handoff prompt** for continuing work in the next session.

He made the skill with the help of Claude, and it is available on **stepanic.domovina.ai** and on his **GitHub**. It is a larger amount of text with instructions. Everything that takes place in the chat is not permanently saved to disk, and Claude learns many details during work: what the pitfalls are, what is still open, and the like. The `/wrap-up` command goes through the entire conversation, records those things, and in the home directory, in the folder for handoffs, creates a file with exact instructions on how to continue.

Why is this useful? Stepanić claims that **Claude is best when it writes prompts to itself**. Such a prompt is optimally structured: it consumes a minimum of tokens, and gives the best result in the next session. This is especially important when working with multiple parallel Claude Code sessions.

He also shared his own observations about the context:
- at the time of the demonstration, the session was consuming **101,000 tokens** out of the available million;
- the first message immediately takes up about **60,000 tokens**, because a multitude of skills and other data are loaded into the context;
- the first 100,000 tokens fill up much faster, and later each message adds only a little;
- if a large amount of one's own knowledge is inserted, the context can grow even to 600,000 tokens;
- the tool is, according to his experience, most effective around **220,000 to 250,000 tokens**, and the next limit he watches out for is 300,000.

He thus divides the work into units. When one is finished and he sees that everything works, he runs wrap-up, then clears the session with the `clear` command. In the new session, he does not have to pass any file: it is enough to say "continue with the last handoff", because he also made a special skill for that.
